<section class="sub-hero"><div class="sub-hero-ph" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/assets/img/photos/roofer.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/roofer-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/roofer.webp 1024w" sizes="100vw" width="1024" height="681" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-parallax="0.18"></div><div class="wrap sub-hero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li><a href="/free-tools/">Free tools</a></li><li aria-current="page">Roof Area &amp; Pitch Calculator</li></ol></nav><p class="kicker">Free calculator</p><h1>Roof Area &amp; Pitch Calculator: A Roof Squares Calculator for Claims</h1><p class="lede">Roof measurements drive most of a hail claim’s value. Use this roof squares calculator to sanity-check the area, pitch and waste on the insurer’s estimate before you accept it.</p></div></section>
<section class="sec tool-sec"><div class="wrap">
<div class="tool" data-tool="roof">
  <div class="tool-head"><span>Roof area &amp; pitch calculator</span><i>Check the squares on your estimate</i></div>
  <div class="tool-body">
    <div class="tool-in">
      <fieldset class="bare"><legend class="sr-only">Measurement method</legend>
        <div class="btn-row">
          <label class="check"><input type="radio" name="mode" value="dims" checked> Footprint length × width</label>
          <label class="check"><input type="radio" name="mode" value="area"> I know the footprint area</label>
        </div></fieldset>
      <div class="row2" data-mode="dims">
        <div><label for="r-l">Footprint length (ft)</label><input id="r-l" name="len" inputmode="decimal" value="52"></div>
        <div><label for="r-w">Footprint width (ft)</label><input id="r-w" name="wid" inputmode="decimal" value="30"></div>
      </div>
      <div data-mode="dims"><label for="r-oh">Eave overhang (inches)</label><input id="r-oh" name="oh" inputmode="decimal" value="16"></div>
      <div data-mode="area" hidden><label for="r-a">Footprint area incl. overhangs (sq ft)</label><input id="r-a" name="area" inputmode="decimal" value="1900"></div>
      <div class="row2">
        <div><label for="r-p">Roof pitch (rise per 12)</label><select id="r-p" name="pitch"><option value="2">2/12</option><option value="3">3/12</option><option value="4">4/12</option><option value="5">5/12</option><option value="6">6/12</option><option value="7" selected>7/12</option><option value="8">8/12</option><option value="9">9/12</option><option value="10">10/12</option><option value="11">11/12</option><option value="12">12/12</option><option value="14">14/12</option><option value="16">16/12</option></select></div>
        <div><label for="r-wst">Waste factor</label><select id="r-wst" name="waste"><option value="10">10% — simple gable</option><option value="12" selected>12% — gable with dormers</option><option value="15">15% — hip roof</option><option value="18">18% — cut-up / complex</option></select></div>
      </div>
      <div><label for="r-pr">Installed price per square (optional)</label><input id="r-pr" name="price" inputmode="decimal" placeholder="e.g. 560"><span class="hint">Use a local contractor’s quote for a rough figure.</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="tool-out" aria-live="polite">
      <div class="out-big"><small>Roof squares (before waste)</small><b data-o="sq">0</b></div>
      <div class="out-rows">
        <div><span>Pitch multiplier</span><b data-o="mult">1.000</b></div>
        <div><span>Roof surface area</span><b data-o="surface">0</b></div>
        <div><span>Squares with waste</span><b data-o="order">0</b></div>
        <div><span>Shingle bundles (3 per square)</span><b data-o="bundles">0</b></div>
        <div><span>Rough replacement cost</span><b data-o="cost">—</b></div>
      </div>
      <p class="out-msg" data-o="steep"></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<p class="tool-note">For planning only. Results depend on the figures you enter and your policy’s terms. They are not a quote, an appraisal or legal advice.</p></div></section><div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose">
<h2>Why measurements move the number</h2>
<p>A roof estimate is priced per square (100 square feet). If the carrier’s estimate is short by a few squares, every line tied to area — tear-off, felt, ice and water shield, shingles, disposal — is short too. On steeper roofs, a missed steep charge can add up quickly.</p>
<h2>How this roof squares calculator works</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Footprint</strong>: length × width plus the overhang on each side, or an area you already have.</li>
<li><strong>Pitch multiplier</strong>: √(1 + (rise ÷ 12)²). A 7/12 roof has about 15% more surface than its footprint.</li>
<li><strong>Waste</strong>: extra material for cuts at hips, valleys and dormers. Complex roofs need more.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Minnesota details to compare</h2>
<p>Minnesota estimates usually include ice and water shield along the eaves, and many older homes have more than one layer of shingles to remove. Check whether your estimate includes additional layers, drip edge and steep or high-roof charges where they apply.</p>
<p>This tool can’t replace a field measurement or aerial report, but it can flag a large mismatch worth questioning. Default dimensions are illustrative.</p>
<h2>Questions about this tool</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>What is a roofing square?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>A square is 100 square feet of roof surface. Estimates price shingles, underlayment and labor per square.</p></div></details><details><summary>Why doesn’t my footprint match the roof area?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Sloped roofs have more surface than the ground area they cover. The pitch multiplier accounts for that, and overhangs add more.</p></div></details><details><summary>What waste factor do insurers use?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>It varies by roof complexity and estimating practice. Simple gables often use around 10%, while hips and cut-up roofs use more.</p></div></details></div><h2>More free tools</h2><div class="related"><a href="/free-tools/percentage-deductible-calculator/"><small>Calculator</small><span>Percentage Deductible Calculator</span><svg class="i" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a><a href="/free-tools/claim-timeline-planner/"><small>Planner</small><span>Claim Timeline Planner</span><svg class="i" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="curr